DIAGNOSTIC: the vendor's exact pattern in CTRL11..CTRL21 of the CSIPHY

WHY
---
It is the last CSIPHY write left untested.

From csiphy_irq_reg_1_2[] of the surya's own Android kernel, at 0x082c..0x0854,
which are exactly the CTRL11..CTRL21 that mainline zeroes:

    FF FF FB FF 7F FF FF EF FF FF FF

Qualcomm calls them interrupt registers and the values look like masks -three of
them with a single bit cleared-, but mainline writes ZERO to all eleven, and at
this point in the investigation it is better to measure than to assume:
everything else in the CSIPHY has been verified register by register against the
vendor and it matches.

0xff on all eleven was already tried (the PHY fires non-stop and not one piece
of data arrives). The exact pattern is what is missing.

    unmask = 0   like mainline, everything zero
                    1   everything 0xff
                    2   the vendor's pattern
